  "methodology": "Original method: premium = (staples Close - Nasdaq Close) / Nasdaq Close * 100; thresholds +/-3% and +/-5%; start in staples; switch only to the opposite ETF. Earn each day's return in the previous holding, then execute at that day's close. Initial capital 10,000 in each pair's own currency; fractional shares; unrebalanced 50/50 benchmark. No dividends, fees, slippage or taxes. Signals and executions at the same close are optimistic and not guaranteed executable.",
  "limitations": "Raw share-price differences are not valuations. Share denominations and splits can dominate signals; Yahoo Close is not dividend-adjusted but is normally split-restated, not historical as-traded prices. No rebasing or reconstruction of as-traded prices is used. Zero-switch results are retained. USD XLP/QQQ does not test XLP against CAD-hedged XQQ; USD and CAD dollar results are separate. Correlations use daily returns, not price levels. Historical performance cannot establish the best future investment. Only XLP is analyzed; IYK, KXI, FSTA and VDC are deferred.",
